# ── Media with unresolved rights — DO NOT COMMIT ────────────────────────────
# These two are excluded on purpose, not by accident. The feature video is
# real-world action-sports footage with the $Send logo composited on; unlike the
# other clips in public/assets (which carry C2PA credentials showing they were
# generated) it carries no authorship metadata at all. The theme audio is a
# bit-exact copy of that video's audio track, so it inherits the same question
# and adds music rights on top.
#
# The repo is intended for a CC0 release, and CC0 is an irrevocable grant to
# everyone — you cannot waive rights you do not hold. Both files stay on disk so
# the site keeps working locally; they simply never enter git.
#
# If you produce a licence that permits sublicensing under a public-domain
# dedication, delete these two lines. Note that GitHub also hard-rejects the
# video for exceeding 100 MB: do NOT "fix" that with Git LFS or by re-encoding,
# because both routes publish the footage.
public/assets/justsendit-full.mp4
public/assets/justsendit-audio.m4a

